      "content": "i've checked for raccoon tracks but i can't find much of anything, just these tiny, almost tiny little indentations in the dirt that don't match any big animal i know. and the way things vanish... it's not like they're being eaten or chewed on, it's like they've just been relocated. like someone moved a heavy watering can a few feet for no reason. do you think there's any kind of pest or creature that actually picks things up and moves them around just to mess with the space? it feels so much more \"deliberate\" than just a squirrel looking for nuts.",
