      "content": "i'll try to get a camera, yeah. but it's just so weird. i went out this morning and found a small pile of shiny pebbles and a few colorful bits of broken glass right in the middle of the patch where my mulch had been moved. it looked almost like... i don't even know, like a little collection was being made? it's so bizarre and honestly since nothing's been eaten, it feels less like biology and more like some kind of weird, tiny prankster is living in my yard. is there any actual scientific explanation for animals \"collecting\" random, non-food objects like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
